{
  "$schema": "./_schema.json",
  "$comment": [
    "Local LLM translation models (GGUF) for the bundled llama-server helper (owned by P4-B; runtime packs in runtime-llama.json, the server in src-tauri/src/services/llm_server/). Family 'mt-llm'; list_llm_models shows them in this order.",
    "Every file is pinned to a Hugging Face commit with its LFS sha256 (from the Hub tree API, as scripts/models/pin-catalog.mjs does). Official Tencent GGUFs for Hy-MT2; community quantizations (mradermacher, the model authors' own repos) elsewhere. Only the text model is used: the mmproj vision files of the Gemma-based models are never downloaded.",
    "min_vram_mb is the whole server on the GPU at the default 4096-token context (weights, KV cache, compute buffers). The Hy-MT2 and MiLMMT numbers equal resources::policy (a test keeps them in step); the others are estimates from the architecture. All are provisional until the P7 campaign measures them; llm_server resizes its VRAM claim to the buffer sizes llama-server reports once it is running.",
    "routing.models: per-model data read by llm_server::catalog with include_str! (not embedded in the model catalog): promptFormat (a TranslationPromptFormat of translation/schema/llm.ts), role (default | challenger | alternative | high_gpu | ab | specialist; specialists are opt-in and never chosen automatically), availability (ok when absent | needs_runtime_update | experimental), kvBytesPerToken (f16 K+V bytes per context token, for contexts above 4096; read from the GGUF header when absent), languages (canonical BCP-47; empty = broadly multilingual), directions (supported pairs when narrower than languages), sampling (the model authors' recommended sampler).",
    "mt/hy-mt2-1.8b-1.25bit needs llama.cpp's STQ1_0 ternary kernel (ggml-org/llama.cpp PR #22836, open and ARM-only as of 2026-09-29): llama-server b11146 cannot load it, so it is listed but never started. mt/madlad400-3b-q4_k_m is a T5 encoder-decoder model; whether llama-server b11146 serves it is unverified (experimental). MiLMMT-46 12B now has a community GGUF (mradermacher, 2026-08); scripts/models/make-gguf.md describes self-conversion for models without one."
  ],
